  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has two arrays AAA and BBB of the same size NNN.\n\nIn one operation, Chef can:\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1≤i≤N)(1 \\leq i \\leq N)(1≤i≤N) and swap the elements AiA_iAi​ and BiB_iBi​.\nChef came up with a task to find the **minimum** possible value of **(Amax−AminA_{max} - A_{min}Amax​−Amin​)** after performing the swap operation any (possibly zero) number of times.\n\nSince Chef is busy, can you help him solve this task?\n\nNote that AmaxA_{max}Amax​ and AminA_{min}Amin​ denote the maximum and minimum elements of the array AAA respectively.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains one integer NNN — the number of elements in each array.\nThe second line consists of NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2,\\ldots ,A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ denoting the elements of the array AAA.\nThe third line consists of NNN space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots ,B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​ denoting the elements of the array BBB.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the **minimum** possible value of **(Amax−AminA_{max} - A_{min}Amax​−Amin​)** in the array AAA after doing swap operation any number of times.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤1091 \\leq A_i, B_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​,Bi​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n1 2\n2 1\n3\n1 5 3\n2 3 1\n4\n4 2 5 1\n5 3 4 1",
        "output": "0\n1\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Chef can make the following operations:\n\nOperation 111: Choose i=1i=1i=1 and swap A1A_1A1​ with B1B_1B1​.\n\nBy doing the above operations, array AAA becomes [2,2][2, 2][2,2]. Here (Amax−Amin)=0(A_{max} - A_{min}) = 0(Amax​−Amin​)=0. It can be shown that this is the minimum value possible.\nTest case 222: Chef can make the following operations:\n\nOperation 111: Choose i=1i=1i=1 and swap A1A_1A1​ with B1B_1B1​.\nOperation 222: Choose i=2i=2i=2 and swap A2A_2A2​ with B2B_2B2​.\n\nBy doing the above operations, array AAA becomes [2,3,3][2, 3, 3][2,3,3]. Here (Amax−Amin)=1(A_{max} - A_{min}) = 1(Amax​−Amin​)=1. It can be shown that this is the minimum value possible.\nTest case 333: Chef can make the following operations:\n\nOperation 111: Choose i=2i=2i=2 and swap A2A_2A2​ with B2B_2B2​.\nOperation 222: Choose i=3i=3i=3 and swap A3A_3A3​ with B3B_3B3​.\n\nBy doing the above operations, array AAA becomes [4,3,4,1][4, 3, 4, 1][4,3,4,1]. Here (Amax−Amin)=3(A_{max} - A_{min}) = 3(Amax​−Amin​)=3. It can be shown that this is the minimum value possible."
      }
    ]
  },
